(4968739, 721572, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by levyj413:</b></div><hr/><i> Ok, I''m a little disappointed your model wasn''t a real Holocaust survivor.  It removes some of the impact for me.  However, as a Jew, I''m very much in favor of anyone who creates imagery that helps the world remember the horror.  Congrats, Enzo! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Generally speaking I would tend to agree with Jeffrey. However since I didn''t see this until now I didn''t confuse it for anything that it''s not. It is a very convincing portrayal of historical significance and a well photographed one at that. Congrats on your red!</td>', 'Originally posted by levyj413: Ok, I''m a little disappointed your model wasn''t a real Holocaust survivor.  It removes some of the impact for me.  However, as a Jew, I''m very much in favor of anyone who creates imagery that helps the world remember the horror.  Congrats, Enzo!   Generally speaking I would tend to agree with Jeffrey. However since I didn''t see this until now I didn''t confuse it for anything that it''s not. It is a very convincing portrayal of historical significance and a well photographed one at that. Congrats on your red!', '2008-09-22 16:26:39.000000', NULL, 0),
